    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="0790" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.0063/1b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Austria-Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-09T11:30:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1917, 11.30 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1646. Austro-Hungarian Chargé d’Affaires here has to-day requested his passports.
                    In accordance with previous instructions, transfer American, British, and
                    Japanese interests to Spanish Ambassador; Roumanian, French, and Italian
                    interests to Swiss Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
